id: para-para-dance
name: Para Para Dance
uaType: both
prerequisite: 2+ Skill Ranks in Performance
tpCost: 10
type: standard
# "Action Cost: Variable (1~3 Actions)", "KP Cost: 4(bT) per Action spent".
actionCost: 1
actionCostMax: 3
kiCostPerBaseTier: 4
kiPerAction: true
# "Using Para Para Dance triggers the Exploit Maneuver from all Opponents who are not at Long Range" - offered on its
# card; an attack through one of them that hits you fails it, its KP given back (chat.mjs paraParaHit). Then its Dance
# button: "Target a number of Opponents up to the number of Actions spent" - your targeted tokens - "Make a Skill Clash
# (Performance vs Performance/Intuition)". Won: Actions lost at the start of their next turn (combat.mjs), 1(bT) off
# their Dodge Rolls for each until then (the Para Para mark).
paraPara: true
exploitable: All Opponents not at Long Range
source: Core Rule
description: >
  1~3 Actions at 4(bT) each: a Skill Clash (Performance vs Performance/Intuition) at that many Opponents - won, they lose
  that many Actions at the start of their next turn, their Dodge 1(bT) lower for each till then. Provokes Exploits; hit
  by one, it fails. Passive: Performance's Critical Target 1 lower.
text: >
  Para Para Dance: Your infectious dance moves act as a form of control, allowing you to force your opponents to jam out
  with you while you handily defeat them.
  –Ability Type: Technical/Magical
  –Prerequisites: 2+ Skill Ranks in Performance
  –TP Cost: 10
  –KP Cost: 4(bT) per Action spent
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: Variable (1~3 Actions)
  –Minions: Non-Minion
  –Passive Bonus: Reduce the Critical Target of your Performance Skill Checks by 1.
  –Effect: Spend up to 3 Actions. Target a number of Opponents up to the number of Actions spent within a Large Sphere
  AoE (centered on you). Make a Skill Clash (Performance vs Performance/Intuition). If you win, on their next turn, that
  Opponent loses an equal number of Actions to the Actions spent on this Unique Ability at the start of their next turn,
  and they cannot convert any Actions into Counter Actions if it would reduce their Actions to less than the amount they
  need to reduce through this effect.

  For each Action an Opponent loses through this effect, reduce their Dodge Rolls by 1(bT) until the start of their next
  turn.

  Using Para Para Dance triggers the Exploit Maneuver form all Opponents who are not at Long Range. If you are hit by an
  Attacking Maneuver made through the Exploit Maneuver when trying to use the Para Para Dance, the Para Para Dance fails
  (you do not regain any spent Actions, but you regain the Ki Points spent on the Para Para Dance).

---

# "Reduce the Critical Target of your Performance Skill Checks by 1." Its Actions owed hold back converting Actions
# into Counter Actions below them (combat.mjs convertibleActions).
[passive]
skill.performance.criticalTarget -= 1;
